      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1188107584,
      "text": "Hibiscus micranthus, the tiny flower hibiscus, is a widespread species of flowering plant in the family Malvaceae. A shrub, it is native to seasonally dry tropical areas of Africa, Madagascar, the Arabian Peninsula, Iran, the Indian Subcontinent, and Myanmar. It is used in traditional medicines."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Hibiscus micranthus",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hibiscus_micranthus",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 160025692,
      "text": "Hibiscus micranthus es una especie de arbusto perteneciente a la familia de las malváceas. Es originaria de África, donde se distribuye por Botsuana, Namibia, Sudáfrica y Yemen."
    }
